{"id":"d7ec29baab92f77c552322603724f7b960b11e5a","axis":"silent","repo":"QwikDev/qwik","sha":"d7ec29baab92f77c552322603724f7b960b11e5a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/deploy-insights.yml","lines":["@@ -59,6 +59,17 @@ jobs:","           ref: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.head_sha }}","           persist-credentials: false"," ","+      - name: Verify deployment credentials","+        if: steps.ownership.outputs.deploy == 'true'","+        env:","+          CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_INSIGHTS_API_TOKEN }}","+          PRIVATE_LIBSQL_DB_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.INSIGHTS_LIBSQL_MIGRATION_TOKEN }}","+        run: |","+          if [ -z \"$CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN\" ] || [ -z \"$PRIVATE_LIBSQL_DB_API_TOKEN\" ]; then","+            echo \"::error::CLOUDFLARE_INSIGHTS_API_TOKEN and INSIGHTS_LIBSQL_MIGRATION_TOKEN are required.\"","+            exit 1","+          fi","+","       - uses: pnpm/action-setup@0ebf47130e4866e96fce0953f49152a61190b271 # v6.0.9","         if: steps.ownership.outputs.deploy == 'true'"," ","@@ -90,15 +101,22 @@ jobs:","         if: steps.ownership.outputs.deploy == 'true'","         run: pnpm -C packages/insights run deploy.dry-run"," ","+      - name: Verify database migration runner","+        if: steps.ownership.outputs.deploy == 'true'","+        run: pnpm -C packages/insights exec vitest run scripts/db.migrate.unit.ts","+","+      - name: Apply Insights database migrations","+        if: steps.ownership.outputs.deploy == 'true'","+        timeout-minutes: 5","+        env:","+          PRIVATE_LIBSQL_DB_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.INSIGHTS_LIBSQL_MIGRATION_TOKEN }}","+        run: pnpm -C packages/insights run db.migrate --production","+","       - name: Deploy Insights to Cloudflare Workers","         if: steps.ownership.outputs.deploy == 'true'","         env:","           CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_INSIGHTS_API_TOKEN }}","         run: |","-          if [ -z \"$CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN\" ]; then","-            echo \"::error::CLOUDFLARE_INSIGHTS_API_TOKEN is required to deploy Insights.\"","-            exit 1","-          fi","           test -f packages/insights/dist/_worker.js","           test -f packages/insights/dist/.assetsignore","           test -f packages/insights/server/entry.cloudflare-pages.js"],"additions":22,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/insights/README.md","lines":["@@ -91,9 +91,10 @@ pnpm -C packages/insights deploy.dry-run"," The separate `Deploy Insights` workflow in `.github/workflows/deploy-insights.yml` owns"," all deployment preparation and publishing. After `Qwik CI` succeeds on `main`, it checks"," out that tested commit, installs locked dependencies, builds Qwik core, the router, the","-ESLint plugin, and Insights, then validates the Cloudflare bundle with a dry run. It","-publishes to Cloudflare and checks that production serves Qwik v2 afterward. Look for","-`Deploy Insights` in the Actions sidebar after `Qwik CI` completes.","+ESLint plugin, and Insights, then validates the Cloudflare bundle with a dry run. It tests","+the migration runner, applies pending database migrations, publishes to Cloudflare, and","+checks that production serves Qwik v2 afterward. A failed migration fails the job and","+prevents publishing. Look for `Deploy Insights` in the Actions sidebar after `Qwik CI` completes."," "," Only successful push or manual `Qwik CI` runs on `main` can trigger publishing. Older commits"," are skipped if `main` has advanced when deployment starts. To retry, rerun the matching","@@ -103,8 +104,21 @@ builds its own bundle and does not depend on artifacts or preparation jobs in `c"," Remove `.github/workflows/deploy-insights.yml` from `v1` before the first v2 deployment;"," the new workflow refuses to publish while that competing workflow exists. Both publishers"," use the same concurrency group so an in-flight deployment finishes before another starts.","-The repository secret `CLOUDFLARE_INSIGHTS_API_TOKEN` supplies the existing Cloudflare","-credentials only to the publishing step. Pull requests never run the deployment job.","+The repository secrets `CLOUDFLARE_INSIGHTS_API_TOKEN` and `INSIGHTS_LIBSQL_MIGRATION_TOKEN`","+are required by the credential preflight. After that check, each is exposed only to its","+publishing or migration step. Pull requests never run the deployment job.","+","+`INSIGHTS_LIBSQL_MIGRATION_TOKEN` must be a dedicated read/write token scoped to the Insights","+database, with schema-change permission. Store it as a GitHub Actions repository secret;","+do not use an organization-wide or database-group token. Production migrations read the","+URL from `wrangler.jsonc`, so they target the same database as the Worker. They ignore local","+`.env` files and require an explicit token. No database credentials enter build artifacts.","+","+The database migration journal makes reruns skip applied migrations. Migrations and publishing","+share the existing production concurrency lock. Keep schema changes backward compatible with","+the currently deployed Worker: migrations run before publishing, and a later publishing failure","+leaves the migrated database in place. Do not roll back the database automatically; retry the","+deployment or ship a forward migration. Validate new migrations against staging first."," "," Keep `PRIVATE_LIBSQL_DB_API_TOKEN`, `PRIVATE_AUTH_SECRET`, and `PRIVATE_GITHUB_SECRET` in"," Cloudflare Worker secrets. For local Workers testing, put the local development values from","@@ -116,8 +130,9 @@ Before promotion:"," "," - Configure the database, session, and GitHub credentials for the target environment. Register","   `https://<deployment-host>/auth/callback/github` as its GitHub OAuth callback.","-- Check the target database's migration history against `drizzle/` and apply any outstanding","-  migrations separately. The manifest compatibility change does not require a schema migration.","+- Check the target database's migration history against `drizzle/`. The production deployment","+  applies pending migrations automatically; use `pnpm -C packages/insights db.migrate` for","+  local or staging credentials."," - Verify sign-in, sign-out, unauthenticated redirects, and per-application access restrictions."," - Exercise application creation and editing, user access changes, dashboard navigation, and","   symbol details in a browser.","@@ -126,3 +141,18 @@ Before promotion:","   responses, including cross-origin browser requests."," - Confirm the rendered page reports the expected `q:version`. Retain the previous Worker version","   for rollback and verify database compatibility before rolling back application code.","+","+## GitHub source previews","+","+Application settings → GitHub source code connects each application to a **public** GitHub","+repository. Set the repository URL, branch/tag/commit, and repository-relative source directory.","+For example, `https://github.com/QwikDev/qwik`, `v1`, and `packages/docs/src` can resolve legacy","+DocSearch origins. Use the revision matching the recorded build; pin a commit for stable results.","+Older manifests may require a different revision. No GitHub credentials are stored or sent.","+","+The source directory is prepended to each symbol's origin. Leave it empty when origins already","+include the full repository-relative path. Clearing the repository disables previews.","+","+The deployment workflow applies `0020_application_source.sql` before publishing this feature.","+It adds `application_sources` and preserves the existing Qwik Docs mapping to `main`; it does","+not guess a revision for historical builds. No existing analytics rows are modified."],"additions":37,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/insights/drizzle/0020_application_source.sql","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@","+CREATE TABLE `application_sources` (","+\t`public_api_key` text PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,","+\t`repository` text NOT NULL,","+\t`revision` text NOT NULL,","+\t`source_root` text NOT NULL,","+\tFOREIGN KEY (`public_api_key`) REFERENCES `applications`(`public_api_key`) ON UPDATE no action ON DELETE no action","+);","+--> statement-breakpoint","+INSERT INTO `application_sources` (`public_api_key`, `repository`, `revision`, `source_root`)","+SELECT `public_api_key`, 'https://github.com/QwikDev/qwik', 'main', 'packages/docs/src'","+FROM `applications` WHERE `public_api_key` = '221smyuj5gl';"],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/insights/drizzle/meta/0020_snapshot.json","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,1863 @@","+{","+  \"version\": \"6\",","+  \"dialect\": \"sqlite\",","+  \"id\": \"31a24dd9-87e4-40e0-89da-b425bf4cbf8e\",","+  \"prevId\": \"c7ff5c52-d899-4ec4-8572-a77cf72295c4\",","+  \"tables\": {","+    \"application_sources\": {","+      \"name\": \"application_sources\",","+      \"columns\": {","+        \"public_api_key\": {","+          \"name\": \"public_api_key\",","+          \"type\": \"text\",","+          \"primaryKey\": true,","+          \"notNull\": true,","+          \"autoincrement\": false","+        },","+        \"repository\": {","+          \"name\": \"repository\",","+          \"type\": \"text\",","+          \"primaryKey\": false,","+          \"notNull\": true,","+          \"autoincrement\": false","+        },","+        \"revision\": {","+          \"name\": \"revision\",","+          \"type\": \"text\",","+          \"primaryKey\": false,","+          \"notNull\": true,","+          \"autoincrement\": false","+        },","+        \"source_root\": {","+          \"name\": \"source_root\",","+          \"type\": \"text\",","+          \"primaryKey\": false,","+          \"notNull\": true,","+          \"autoincrement\": false","+        }","+      },","+      \"indexes\": {},","+      \"foreignKeys\": {","+        \"application_sources_public_api_key_applications_public_api_key_fk\": {","+          \"name\": \"application_sources_public_api_key_applications_public_api_key_fk\",","+    